\paragraph{Exponential Factor:}
We now compute the ``exponential factor'' in~\eqref{eq:ExtenstionFormula_Expression}, which we denote by
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:exp_factor}
\begin{aligned}
E_{\operatorname{exp}}:\mathbb R^N\times U&\to\mathbb R^N,\\
E_{\operatorname{exp}}(u_1,\ldots,u_N,x)
&\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}
\left(
\exp\left[
\frac{1}{1-s}
\left(
\frac{u_i}{MR(x)^{s+1}}
+
A_s\left(\frac{|x-X_i|}{R(x)}\right)^{2s}
\right)
\right]
\right)_{i=1}^N,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $U\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}\mathbb R^d\setminus\{X_1,\ldots,X_N\}$.

We now formalize the $\mathbb{G}$-circuit in~\eqref{fig:ExpFactor}.  
Consider the DAG of subcircuits $\mathcal C_{\exp:N}\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}(V,E,(g_v)_{v\in V})$, with input vertices $w_j$ carrying $u_j$, input block $v_0$ carrying $x$, and designated outputs $(v_{9,j})_{j=1}^N$, where
$$
\begin{aligned}
V
&=\{v_0,r_0,r_1,r_2,r_3\}
\cup\{w_j:j\in[N]\}
\cup\{v_{i,j}:i\in[9],\,j\in[N]\},\\
E
&=\{(v_0,r_0),(r_0,r_1),(r_0,r_2),(r_2,r_3)\}\\
&\quad\cup\{(v_{i,j},v_{i+1,j}):i\in[4],\,j\in[N]\}\\
&\quad\cup\bigcup_{j=1}^N
\bigl\{
(v_0,v_{1,j}),(r_1,v_{3,j}),
(w_j,v_{6,j}),(r_3,v_{6,j}),
(v_{5,j},v_{7,j}),(v_{6,j},v_{7,j}),
(v_{7,j},v_{8,j}),(v_{8,j},v_{9,j})
\bigr\}.
\end{aligned}
$$
Assign the maps
$$
g_v=
\begin{cases}
\operatorname{Id}_{\mathbb R^d},&v=v_0,\\
\operatorname{Id}_{\mathbb R},&v=w_j,\\
R,&v=r_0,\\
1/\cdot,&v\in\{r_1,r_3\},\\
M(\cdot)^{s+1},&v=r_2,\\
\cdot-X_j,&v=v_{1,j},\\
|\cdot|,&v=v_{2,j},\\
\end{cases}
\quad \dots \mbox{ and } \dots \quad
g_v=
\begin{cases}
\times_2,&v\in\{v_{3,j},v_{6,j}\},\\
\cdot^{2s},&v=v_{4,j},\\
A_s\cdot,&v=v_{5,j},\\
+_2,&v=v_{7,j},\\
\frac{1}{1-s}\cdot,&v=v_{8,j},\\
\exp,&v=v_{9,j}.
\end{cases}
$$
The shared vertices $r_1$ and $r_3$ evaluate to $1/R(x)$ and $1/(MR(x)^{s+1})$, respectively. Thus $v_{5,j}$ evaluates to $A_s(|x-X_j|/R(x))^{2s}$, while $v_{6,j}$ evaluates to $u_j/(MR(x)^{s+1})$. The final addition, scaling, and exponential therefore give $f_{\mathcal C_{\exp:N}}=E_{\operatorname{exp}}$ on $\mathbb R^N\times U$. Every division is admissible since $R(x)>0$ on $U$. After expanding the sub-circuits, the depth is $\mathcal O(\log d+\log N)$, and the width and size are $\mathcal O(dN)$.


